# DTF tier manifest: scan-on-proxy-maven-nuget  (artifact-keeper 1.11.0:
# #4100 Maven/Gradle/sbt, #4102 NuGet, #3603 nuspec identity, #4099 formats)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the mock-scan-formats upstream. LOCAL-ONLY: the
# verdicts come from the backend image's bundled Grype and its pre-seeded
# vulnerability DB (no scanner sidecar, no OSV, no internet), graded over
# fixtures whose own manifests name long-published advisories.
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS: before 1.11.0 a Maven or NuGet Remote with
# scan_on_proxy=true streamed every proxied package unscanned (200, no
# X-AK-Scan), whatever proxy_scan_action said. 1.11.0 routes .jar/.war/.ear
# (Maven) and .nupkg (NuGet V3 flat container and V2 package route) through
# the shared inline scan gate: vulnerable -> 403 scan_blocked, clean -> 200
# X-AK-Scan: clean, identity that the package's own manifest does not back ->
# 423 under fail_closed, .sha1 sidecar mismatch -> 502 and evicted, ambiguous
# paths -> 400 before any upstream fetch; and /api/v1/formats reports which
# formats enforce the gate.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.10.0. Green: ak-backend:1.11.0 and newer.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: admin setup plus ~30 back-to-back pulls.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock sits on a private per-slot subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-scan-formats"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
